### Demo data: mvn quarkus:dev
### or Docker: orgkeep-examples/docker-compose, docker compose up -d (port 8284 instead of 8282)
### Accounts (realm "demo"), password "password": realm-owner, org-owner (owner of the organisation "acme"),
### org-user, paul (team sales) and emma (team accounting)
### Tokens: login client of the realm (clientId = realm name), password grant enabled for the demo by DemoSeeder

### Token of the realm owner
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=realm-owner
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password

> {%
    client.global.set("realm_owner_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### Token of the owner of acme
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=org-owner
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password

> {%
    client.global.set("org_owner_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### Token of org-user (Claire): the default catalog "products" is a default scope of the login client,
### resource_access.products has billing, given by the team users
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=org-user
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password

### Token of paul, team sales, catalog prod only: resource_access.prod has billing:stats, billing:search, shop:write,
### shop:search (no access role for a metered product). In the claim "prod", an object per metered feature:
### prod.shop.search.quotas has the pool of acme ("/"), prod.billing.search.quotas also the pool "/sales" (50 a day),
### the quota of team of sales for this feature
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=paul
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password
    &scope=openid prod

### Token of emma, team accounting, catalog prod only: every feature of billing, prod.billing.search and prod.billing.dig
### with the pool of acme each
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=emma
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password
    &scope=openid prod

### Token of paul, catalog sandbox only: larger quotas, and the API of prod refuses it (prod is not in aud)
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo
    &username=paul
    &password=password
    &grant_type=password
    &scope=openid sandbox

### Realm owner: list organisations
GET http://localhost:8282/api/admin/organisations
Authorization: Bearer {{realm_owner_token}}

### Org owner: list the members of acme
GET http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/members
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}

### Org owner: add a member to acme
POST http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/members
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@acme.test",
  "firstName": "Bob",
  "lastName": "Smith"
}

### Org owner: the teams of acme, with what they give
GET http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/user-groups
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}

### Org owner: the products of acme, to configure the teams
GET http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/products
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}

### Org owner: the team sales also gets dig on billing in prod, with a quota of team for dig too. Giving the product
### again replaces what the team gives of it: the quota of search is sent again to keep it
PUT http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/user-groups/sales/products/prod/billing
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "features": ["stats", "search", "dig"],
  "featureQuotas": {
    "search": { "quota": 50, "cycle": "DAILY" },
    "dig": { "quota": 20 }
  }
}

### Org owner: the catalog roles of prod the teams can give
GET http://localhost:8282/api/organisations/acme/catalogs/prod/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}

### Org owner: forbidden on the realm owner endpoints (403)
GET http://localhost:8282/api/admin/organisations
Authorization: Bearer {{org_owner_token}}
